iety i don't want us to  suppress them  i don't want us to get rid of them i  want us to listen to them  and not just allow these feelings any of  those things will just make  it worse and as i said it'll come back  our anxiety for me is a sign that we  care and that we're alive and we're  awake  and we need to pay attention to that  it's a sign of empathy  without empathy and that compassion both  for ourselves and for others  particularly with these global crises  that we're dealing with now  we would not be alive or awake or  engaged as human beings  for more debates talks and interviews  subscribe  today to the institute of art and ideas  at iai tv  you

